        "description": "## Update User\n\nUpdates an existing user in the Petstore system.\n\nThis request performs a **full update** of a user record identified by username.\n\n---\n\n## Endpoint\n\n`PUT {{petstoreBaseUrl}}/v2/user/{{user2_username}}`\n\n### Variables\n\n| Variable | Source | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `{{petstoreBaseUrl}}` | environment/collection | Base URL for the Petstore API (for example, `https://petstore.swagger.io`) |\n| `{{user2_username}}` | environment | The username of the user to update (path parameter) |\n\n---\n\n## Authentication\n\nThis endpoint typically uses **no auth** in the public Swagger Petstore deployment.\n\nIf your Petstore instance requires authentication, configure it at the request/collection level (for example, API key or bearer token) and keep the same request shape.\n\n---\n\n## Request Body (JSON)\n\nSend a JSON object representing the user.\n\n### Fields\n\n| Field | Type | Required | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `id` | integer | yes | Numeric identifier for the user |\n| `username` | string | yes | Username value stored for the user (can match the path username depending on implementation) |\n| `firstName` | string | no | User first name |\n| `lastName` | string | no | User last name |\n| `email` | string | no | Email address |\n| `password` | string | no | Password value |\n| `phone` | string | no | Phone number |\n| `userStatus` | integer | no | User status (implementation-specific) |\n\n### Example body\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"id\": 888,\n  \"username\": \"John\",\n  \"firstName\": \"Johnson\",\n  \"lastName\": \"Dmiriti\",\n  \"email\": \"JohnsonDmitri@gmail.com\",\n  \"password\": \"Olympi@666\",\n  \"phone\": \"Olympi@666\",\n  \"userStatus\": 1\n}\n\n ```\n\n---\n\n## Expected Responses\n\n### 200 OK (Success)\n\nUser updated successfully.\n\nExample response:\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"code\": 200,\n  \"type\": \"unknown\",\n  \"message\": \"888\"\n}\n\n ```\n\nNotes:\n\n- `message` commonly contains the updated user `id` as a string.\n    \n\n### 404 Not Found\n\nReturned when the specified user cannot be found.\n\nExample response (shape may vary by deployment):\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"code\": 404,\n  \"type\": \"unknown\",\n  \"message\": \"User not found\"\n}\n\n ```\n\n---\n\n## Quick usage example\n\nSet variables (in the active environment **AI DEMO**):\n\n- `petstoreBaseUrl`\n    \n- `user2_username`\n    \n\nThen send the request with a JSON body containing the updated user fields."
